# No object / Any typing

Never use `object`, `typing.Any`, bare `dict`, bare `list`, or bare `tuple` as types.

## Required

- Prefer `TypedDict`, `dataclass`, `NamedTuple`, enums, and unions (`str | None`)
- Annotate every public function parameter and return type
- Use `dict[str, str]`, `list[Concrete]`, `tuple[Concrete, ...]`, etc.
- One class / TypedDict / enum per file when practical
